WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.370
My first anatomy lesson was not a drawing. A fox lay

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:07.264
on the table. I wanted to understand how its parts

00:00:07.264 --> 00:00:08.190
worked together.

00:00:09.592 --> 00:00:13.328
Later, I brought a microscope from Cairo to Qatar. At

00:00:13.328 --> 00:00:16.671
home, curiosity did not have to wait for laboratory

00:00:16.671 --> 00:00:17.064
hours.

00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:21.447
We began with plant extracts and questions about

00:00:21.447 --> 00:00:22.689
medicinal chemistry.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.241
Some experiments were simple. The answers were rarely

00:00:26.241 --> 00:00:26.911
as simple.

00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:31.960
Imine synthesis and molecular sensing taught me to

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:32.532
distrust

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:36.079
a beautiful explanation until I could interrogate the

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:36.681
spectrum.

00:00:38.175 --> 00:00:41.873
We built a student chemistry community. Science grew

00:00:41.873 --> 00:00:42.513
in shared

00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:45.289
laboratories, long arguments, and the people who

00:00:45.289 --> 00:00:46.851
challenged our assumptions.

00:00:48.342 --> 00:00:51.916
A polymer would not behave as planned. I learned how

00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:54.945
little a plausible structure tells us about a real

00:00:54.945 --> 00:00:55.490
material.

00:00:56.883 --> 00:01:00.055
Then I began following developing vessels in

00:01:00.055 --> 00:01:01.064
zebrafish. The

00:01:01.064 --> 00:01:04.199
organism moved, blood flowed, and measurement became a

00:01:04.199 --> 00:01:05.244
different problem.

00:01:06.675 --> 00:01:10.358
An embedding attempt failed when agarose and paraffin

00:01:10.358 --> 00:01:11.331
would not hold

00:01:11.331 --> 00:01:14.648
together. The microtome exposed a materials problem,

00:01:14.648 --> 00:01:15.988
not a usable section.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:20.989
In the lung, we studied what happens when an

00:01:20.989 --> 00:01:23.546
airway reopens and a moving interface injures

00:01:23.546 --> 00:01:24.512
epithelial cells.

00:01:25.883 --> 00:01:29.212
Biomaterials and engineered surfaces added another

00:01:29.212 --> 00:01:31.010
constraint: a substance can

00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:34.948
be chemically interesting yet behave very differently

00:01:34.948 --> 00:01:36.137
at an interface.

00:01:37.675 --> 00:01:41.117
Now I study dexamethasone vesicles intended for

00:01:41.117 --> 00:01:42.655
inhalation. A carrier

00:01:42.655 --> 00:01:46.093
must withstand nebulization before it can even be

00:01:46.093 --> 00:01:47.636
assessed for delivery.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:52.332
I also study how earlier pharmacists made medicines

00:01:52.332 --> 00:01:54.088
dependable. Across centuries

00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:57.804
and disciplines, I keep returning to what the evidence

00:01:57.804 --> 00:01:59.042
can actually bear.
